      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "mimir"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(leios_logmetrics_txgen_bytes_total{environment=\"leios\", service=\"tx-firehose\"}[${window}s])) / 1000",
          "legendFormat": "submitted (all firehoses)",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "mimir"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(leios_logmetrics_txgen_submitted_total{environment=\"leios\", service=\"tx-centrifuge\"}[${window}s])) * 204 / 1000",
          "legendFormat": "submitted (all centrifuges, est. 204 B/tx)",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "mimir"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "clamp_min(deriv(cardano_node_metrics_mempoolBytes_int{job=\"integrations/cardano-node\", environment=\"leios\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[${window}s]), 0) / 1000",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} mempool throughput",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Submission vs. mempool",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "description": "Submitted throughput per generator. Firehose bytes are the measured on-wire size (txgen_bytes_total); tx-centrifuge has no on-wire size, so its bytes are ESTIMATED at 204 B/tx (submitted-rate x 204). The mempool series is the derivative of mempoolBytes, clamped at 0 so draining (a block being forged) reads as no fill rather than as negative throughput. Submission is bursty when the mempool stalls, so widen the rate window before reading a level off this panel. The mempool series measures accumulation, not ingest: a node keeping up shows ~0. Use 'Ingest vs. submitted' to see whether a node can keep up."
    },
