          "range": true,
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Ingest vs. submitted (tx/s)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "description": "What each node can actually take in from its peers, against the load being offered. A node that is keeping up sits on the submitted line; one that cannot sits below it, and the gap is the diffusion shortfall. Note relay11 (or whichever node the generators target) reads zero here: it ingests over node-to-client, which does not go through tx-submission at all. Contrast with the mempool series on 'Submission vs. mempool', which measures accumulation — a node keeping up perfectly shows ~0 there."
    }
